  "hint": "Eunomia has no model configured, so you review the ontology. Read the profile: each kind and link type with its counts and sample names, and each kind's properties. Then call `ontology_propose` with a one-sentence description for each kind and link type that has none, the kinds that name the same thing as another (`merge_into` the one to keep), the link types worth keeping, the typed properties the kinds' facts show (`properties`: kind, name, datatype, unit), and the metrics those properties can compute (`metrics`: kind, name, description, expr such as {\"agg\": \"avg\", \"property\": \"price\"}, or a per-entity `row` such as {\"agg\": \"sum\", \"row\": {\"op\": \"mul\", \"left\": \"stock\", \"right\": \"cost\"}}). Give a kind or property `synonyms` only when the vault's own names or facts spell them out. A vault owner approves or rejects proposals in the Eunomia app.",
